Dawnmonger is an inventor who travels with [[People/Althane/Lev|Lev]], [[People/Althane/Henrik|Henrik]] and [[People/Althane/Divex|Divex]] as [[Org/Althane/The Weft|the Weft]]. He builds and repairs machines, and wears a pair of rocket boots he made himself. He worked out how the [[Phenomena/Althane/Clockwork Rejuvenator|clockwork rejuvenator]] is built from studying the one the Weft had made in [[Geography/Althane/The Hollow/Lava Ruin/index|the lava ruin]].

He carries the chrome of [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)|Syrin]] in his skull and neck.

He is called the greatest inventor on Althane, and says so himself. His work runs on the power of a [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessian]]: he designed the [[Phenomena/Althane/Dawn Engine|Dawn engine]], and the one the Weft built in [[Geography/Althane/Lunae Badlands/Hidden Gulch/New Haven|New Haven]] drains the Beast that lies in the blood lake there.

After [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/The Deep|the Deep]] was destroyed, Dawnmonger walked Althane for years, chronicling what he saw and writing down improvements to his engines, then left the plans with [[People/Althane/Marzo|Marzo]] and joined Lev in mapping [[Phenomena/Althane/The Lighthouse|the Lighthouse]] and the anchorways.
